{"title":"Resilient overnight runner: durable resume, bounded supervision, real soak evidence","objective":"Close the four evidenced gaps in the overnight run (no restart/supervision, no resume of an interrupted run, 120min/5-session default budget at runtime/atl-manager.mjs:417-418, no unattended real-provider soak test) while preserving the existing safeguards documented at USAGE.md:136 — --confirm gate, durable ledger at .trust/manager/overnight/run.json, one global slot, and the never-replay-an-in-flight-session rule.","constraints":["Human gate is non-negotiable: overnight/run require --confirm (runtime/atl-manager.mjs:398-400); no unattended merge, deploy, policy, spending, or external messaging (USAGE.md:136).","Never replay an in-flight provider session; recovery continues only untouched tasks from the last durable boundary (USAGE.md:136). Resume work must checkpoint at session boundaries only.","Budget caps stay: --max-minutes 1..1440, --max-sessions 1..20 (runtime/atl-manager.mjs:419-423); 'whole night' means configurable defaults up to the existing caps, not new unlimited modes.","ATL does not install scheduled tasks itself; supervision ships as a command users start manually, plus a Task Scheduler command plan (USAGE.md:136).","Auth policy holds: subscription mode strips provider env vars and never falls back to API; --auth api only when intentional (USAGE.md:136).","The documented host constraint (an AI session must remain open; open laptop alone is insufficient) is a provider/CLI fact — scope is to document it and add power-settings/scheduler command plans, not to claim it is removed.","Ledger writes must be atomic (temp file + rename) so a crash cannot corrupt run.json mid-write.","Real-provider soak test costs tokens and runs unattended: it must be human-initiated, tiny-budget, and skipped by default in automated runs."],"risks":[{"risk":"Auto-restart becomes an unattended loop that burns budget without a fresh human decision","mitigation":"Watchdog requires --confirm once up front, enforces a hard --max-restarts cap, re-checks remaining time/session budget before every relaunch, and exits when budget or blockers are exhausted"},{"risk":"Resume accidentally replays the interrupted in-flight session and double-spends provider tokens","mitigation":"Keep the interrupted session excluded from recovery exactly as today; tests assert the interrupted task id is never re-spawned"},{"risk":"Crash during ledger write leaves truncated run.json that recovery silently trusts","mitigation":"Atomic writes plus a test feeding a truncated ledger; status must report quarantine and refuse resume"},{"risk":"Soak test runs accidentally in CI and spends real tokens","mitigation":"Requires explicit --confirm plus an env acknowledgement, uses a 15-minute/2-session budget, and is excluded from default verifier invocations"},{"risk":"Windows-only supervision breaks on other hosts or after laptop sleep","mitigation":"Implement as a plain Node script with no OS service dependency; document sleep/power plan; offline tests use a fake worker stub, not a real CLI"}],"completion_checks":[{"check":"verification/recovery_test.mjs passes including the new cases: remaining-task resume, interrupted-session non-replay, truncated-ledger quarantine","evidence":"test exit code 0 with the new case names present in output"},{"check":"verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py reconciles with the updated recovery states","evidence":"model run exits 0 against config/manager-state-contract.json"},{"check":"atl overnight honors configured overnight budget defaults from config/manager.json with CLI flags overriding and caps still enforced","evidence":"unit test asserting 120/5 fallback when unset, override when set, StateError above 1440/20"},{"check":"--confirm gate is intact after the change","evidence":"a non-dry-run overnight invocation without --confirm throws the existing StateError; grep shows the guard still precedes any spawn"},{"check":"Offline supervision test: killing the fake worker mid-queue leads to at most --max-restarts relaunches, each preceded by recover, never exceeding remaining budget","evidence":"new verification test exit 0"},{"check":"One human-executed real-provider soak run produced a run.json showing a mid-run kill and successful recovery of remaining tasks within a 15-minute/2-session budget","evidence":"the soak artifact under .trust/manager/overnight/ plus the test's summary line; this check is complete only when that run has actually happened"},{"check":"USAGE.md:136 overnight section and docs pages reflect resume, watchdog, and soak usage without weakening the session-must-stay-open statement","evidence":"docs grep shows the new commands documented; docs sync output clean"}],"acceptance_examples":[{"example":"An overnight run with a 5-session budget is killed by a laptop crash after session 2 completes and session 3 is in flight. Morning: atl overnight status shows 2 completed, 1 interrupted (excluded), 2 pending; atl overnight recover --confirm completes sessions from the durable boundary within the remaining budget; the interrupted session id never appears again in the ledger as spawned."},{"example":"run.json is found truncated after a hard power-off. atl overnight status reports a quarantine reason instead of resuming, and recover refuses with a human-readable error until the operator archives the corrupt file."},{"example":"The operator starts atl overnight watch --confirm --max-restarts 2 --max-minutes 480 --max-sessions 20 before bed. The runner process dies once at session 1; the watchdog runs recover --confirm, relaunches once, and finishes. A second death consumes the second restart; a third death makes the watchdog exit with a summary instead of looping."},{"example":"Overnight budgets come from config/manager.json (e.g. maxMinutes 480, maxSessions 16); a CLI --max-minutes 30 overrides for one run; --max-minutes 2000 is rejected by the existing cap. A repo with no config still gets today's 120/5."},{"example":"A human runs node verification/overnight_soak_test.mjs --confirm against the configured zai provider with a 15-minute/2-session budget; the harness kills the runner once mid-session, recovery completes the queue, and the test prints a pass/fail summary with the ledger path. CI invocations without the acknowledgement skip it."}],"selected_skills":[{"skill":"agent-trust-ladder","reason":"Provides the SDD/TDD ladder (frame → specify → plan → implement → verify) this plan is shaped into"},{"skill":"atl-pip","reason":"Implementation worker for the runtime changes (recovery, budget config, watchdog) in a self-correcting loop"},{"skill":"atl-beacon","reason":"Verifier / night-watch role: owns the verifier-command pass and is the natural operator role for the human-gated soak run"}],"proposed_worker":{"implementer":"pip","verifier":"beacon","coordinator":"mira (optional; single-task scope, pip + beacon suffice)","notes":"One global slot means implementation and the soak run must be sequential; soak runs last, after offline tests pass."},"implementation_steps":[{"step":1,"title":"Baseline evidence, no changes","detail":"Record current behavior: read the ledger/recovery code paths (runtime/lib/recovery.mjs, runtime/lib/state.mjs, overnight sections of runtime/atl-manager.mjs), run the existing recovery/intake/dashboard tests and the lifecycle model, and capture today's ledger schema. No edits in this step."},{"step":2,"title":"TDD: durable resume of an interrupted run","detail":"First add failing cases to verification/recovery_test.mjs: (a) after a mid-queue kill, recover --confirm continues remaining untouched tasks within remaining time/session budget; (b) the interrupted in-flight session is recorded and never re-spawned; (c) a truncated run.json is quarantined, status reports it, recover refuses. Then implement: atomic ledger writes (temp+rename) in runtime/lib/state.mjs or recovery.mjs and a resume path in runtime/atl-manager.mjs that carries remaining budget forward. Keep the gate and no-replay invariants."},{"step":3,"title":"TDD: configurable overnight budget defaults","detail":"Add a failing test that overnight budgets default from config/manager.json (new overnightBudget field), fall back to the current 120/5 (runtime/atl-manager.mjs:417-418) when absent, are overridden by CLI flags, and still hit the 1..1440 / 1..20 caps. Implement in parseWorkerFlags plus config load; update verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py and config/manager-state-contract.json to cover the new states."},{"step":4,"title":"TDD: bounded supervision command","detail":"Add a failing offline test using a fake worker stub: atl overnight watch --confirm --max-restarts N relaunches the runner after process exit, runs recover --confirm between attempts, decrements remaining budget before each relaunch, and exits after N restarts, budget exhaustion, or blockers. Implement as a Node command (runtime/atl-manager.mjs plus runtime/lib/recovery.mjs or a new small lib) with no OS service dependency and no scheduled-task installation; emit the Task Scheduler command plan for users who want one."},{"step":5,"title":"Human-gated real-provider soak test","detail":"Add verification/overnight_soak_test.mjs: tiny budget (15 minutes / 2 sessions) against the configured provider, kills the runner once mid-session, then asserts recovery completes the queue. Requires --confirm and an explicit env acknowledgement; without them it prints the skip reason and exits 0 so default suites stay offline. Do not execute it as part of the plan; a human with a funded provider runs it once and archives the run.json evidence."},{"step":6,"title":"Docs and sync","detail":"Update the overnight paragraph at USAGE.md:136 (resume, watch, soak, budget config) while keeping the session-must-stay-open statement intact; mirror into README.md/runtime/README.md and the docs pages that cover overnight, then run the docs sync step."},{"step":7,"title":"Full verifier pass","detail":"Run every verifier command below against the finished diff; record outputs as evidence. The real-provider soak from step 5 is the only check that may remain pending, and it must be labeled as such rather than claimed."}],"verifier_commands":["node verification/recovery_test.mjs","node verification/intake_test.mjs","node verification/dashboard_test.mjs","python -I verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py","node runtime/atl-manager.mjs overnight --dry-run","node runtime/atl-manager.mjs overnight <task-id> 2>&1 | grep -q \"requires --confirm\"","node verification/overnight_soak_test.mjs --dry-run"]}
